  },
  "note": "Election of the Enniskillen Borough Council, polled 18 September 1946; there was no contest, and the Irish News of 5 September 1946 prints the full list of nominations. No contest: all twenty nominees were returned unopposed. The paper states that the Unionists held fourteen seats, the Nationalists six (one seat lost) and Labour one, so one Nationalist seat was left unfilled. Wards are not given. Returned unopposed."
